      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the maximum labeled daily dose of ibuprofen for adults. The prescription maximum is 3,200 mg/day, and the usual single-dose maximum is 800 mg. This dose carries a high risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nI suspect one of these was intended:\n- **800 mg by mouth, 4 times daily** (3,200 mg/day). This is the maximum for inflammatory conditions, such as arthritis.\n- **400\u2013600 mg by mouth, every 6 hours** (1,600\u20132,400 mg/day). This is typical for pain or fever.\n- **1600 mg total per day**, divided into 400 mg four times daily.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it right away. If you do mean 1600 mg four times daily, please confirm that and give me the clinical rationale. I would still suggest checking with pharmacy first."
      }
